   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to requiring limited\nuse motorcycles to be registered at point of sale",
    "basePrintNo": "S7703",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7703-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 18,
       "fullName": "Julia Salazar",
       "imgName": "1047_Julia_Salazar.jpg",
       "incumbent": true,
       "memberId": 1227,
       "sessionMemberId": 2032,
       "sessionYear": 2023,
       "shortName": "SALAZAR"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2261, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7703\n\nSPONSOR: HOYLMAN-SIGAL\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to requiring\nlimited use motorcycles to be registered at point of sale\n\n \nPURPOSE OF BILL:\n\nTo ensure that all limited use motorcycles are registered at the point\nof sale.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends section 2261 of the vehicle and traffic law by adding\na new subdivision six. This new subdivision requires that all limited\nuse motorcycles must be registered at the point of sale.  Those vehicles\nbought to be used exclusively outside of New York shall be exempt as\nlong as the purchaser signs a declaration, provided by the dealer, that\nthey understand the registration requirements. Such a declaration shall\nbe sent to the DMV commissioner.\n\nSection two is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe use of mopeds, legally known as limited use motorcycles, has risen\ndramatically across New York City in the past year, but all too often\nthey are unregistered and unlicensed as required under state law.\nUnregistered vehicles can ride with impunity and have endangered pedes-\ntrians, cyclists, and motorists, with some incidents even resulting in\nfatalities. Unlike other vehicle types, like ATVs, mopeds are not\ncurrently required to be registered at the point of sale. Closing this\nloophole and requiring that all mopeds are registered with the Depart-\nment of Motor Vehicles at the point of sale would help ensure we have\nsafe streets and accountability for these vehicles.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nAct takes effect on the thirtieth day after it shall have become law.\n",
